  "Question": "The arithmetic mean of a set of \\(50\\) numbers is \\(38.\\) If two numbers of the set, namely \\(45\\) and \\(55,\\) are discarded, the arithmetic mean of the remaining set of numbers is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(38.5\\)",
    "B": "\\(37.5\\)",
    "C": "\\(37\\)",
    "D": "\\(36.5\\)",
    "E": "\\(36\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "An arithmetic mean is the sum divided by the number of values, so the original sum is\n\\[\n 50\\cdot38=1900.\n\\]\nDiscarding \\(45\\) and \\(55\\) removes \\(100\\) from this sum and leaves \\(50-2=48\\) numbers. Their mean is therefore\n\\[\n \\frac{1900-45-55}{48}\n =\\frac{1800}{48}\n =37.5.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(37.5\\), choice B.",
